.swimmer.ammonite svg { animation: drift 3s ease-in-out infinite alternate; }
.swimmer.turtle svg { animation: paddle 1.4s ease-in-out infinite; }
.swimmer.school .face { position: relative; width: 50px; height: 20px; }
.fish { position: absolute; animation: drift 1.2s ease-in-out infinite alternate; }
.fish:nth-child(2n) { animation-delay: -.6s; }
.swimmer.frantic svg, .swimmer.frantic .fish { animation: frantic .14s ease-in-out infinite alternate !important; }
@keyframes frantic { from { transform: translateY(-2px) rotate(-6deg); } to { transform: translateY(2px) rotate(6deg); } }
/* flying and wading Quetzalcoatlus always sits in front of the water */
.beast.flyer { z-index: 4; }
.face svg.stand { display: none; }
.beast.perched { bottom: 72px; }
.beast.perched .face svg:first-child { display: none; }
.beast.perched .face svg.stand { display: block; animation: breathe 3s ease-in-out infinite; }
.beast.perched.snatch .face svg.stand { transform-origin: 40% 100%; animation: snatch 1.3s ease-in-out 1; }
@keyframes snatch { 0%,100% { transform: rotate(0); } 35%,55% { transform: rotate(24deg) translateY(4px); } }
</style>
<script src="https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/[email]/plotly.min.js"></script>

<div class="wrap">
  <header>
    <h1>K-Pg Impact Winter<span class="preview-tag">Preview</span></h1>
    <p>How much did the asteroid impact 66 million years ago disrupt climate and life? <span class="chain">Haze &rarr; sunlight &rarr; temperature &rarr; photosynthesis &rarr; food web.</span></p>
  </header>

  <section class="console" aria-label="Simulation controls">
    <span class="console-label">Simulation controls</span>
    <label class="toggle"><input type="checkbox" id="soot" checked><span class="track"></span>
      <span>Soot<small>from global wildfires</small></span></label>
    <label class="toggle"><input type="checkbox" id="sulf" checked><span class="track"></span>
      <span>Sulfate<small>from vaporized rock</small></span></label>
    <button id="run" type="button">Run simulation</button>
    <div class="showing" aria-live="polite">Showing: <b id="showing">Soot + sulfate</b></div>
  </section>

  <div class="main">
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="chart"><h2>Sunlight at surface<span>% of normal</span></h2><div class="plot" id="p-trans"></div></div>
      <div class="chart"><h2>Surface temperature<span>&deg;C, global mean</span></h2><div class="plot" id="p-Ts"></div></div>
      <div class="chart"><h2>Photosynthesis<span>% of normal</span></h2><div class="plot" id="p-prod"></div></div>
      <div class="chart"><h2>Food web<span>biomass, % of normal (log scale)</span></h2><div class="plot" id="p-web"></div></div>
    </div>
    <aside>
      <div class="term" aria-label="Model output"><pre id="term"></pre></div>
      <div class="notes">
        <h3>Reading the graphs</h3>
        <p>The time axis stretches the first year (monthly steps), then counts years on a log scale out to 60. Hover for exact values.</p>
        <p>The dashed gray line is the no-impact control. It stays flat at 15 &deg;C (288 K), which checks that the model is balanced before the impact.</p>
        <h3>The animals</h3>
        <p>The animals at the bottom are a drawing of the model's herbivore and predator levels. The herd size follows each level's lowest point: a full herd is 8 herbivores and 6 predators (assumed sizes), times the lowest biomass fraction, with at least 1 survivor. The ferns, trees and the green plankton dots in the sea follow the producers level the same way. The small sea animals (fish, ammonites, belemnites, baby turtles) follow the herbivore level: at its lowest point, missing trees stand dead and missing ferns leave bare ground. When one animal wanders off, another kind from the same level walks on, so the count stays the same. All five kinds lived at the impact. <i>Quetzalcoatlus</i> is a flying pterosaur and the plesiosaur and <i>Mosasaurus</i> are marine reptiles. None of these three is a dinosaur.</p>
        <p>This is a simple global-mean model. Its three food-web levels are generic groups, not counts of any species.</p>
        <p><span class="dim">Preview built from <code>run()</code> with the default scenario (soot &tau; = 8.0, lasting 1.5 yr; sulfate &tau; = 2.0, lasting 3.0 yr). The real site will read <code>data.json</code>.</span></p>
      </div>

